&lt;p&gt;Discord runs one of the largest real-time audio/video platforms in the world, and this role encompasses all the infrastructure required to make this happen at Discord&#39;s massive scale. Your work will directly impact Discord&#39;s core experience, contributing to what makes over 200 million monthly users love the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Audio/Video Infrastructure team oversees every voice call, video call, and Go Live session. You&#39;ll lead the team responsible for writing the software that routes all data and manages thousands of machines to create a seamless user experience. Your responsibilities will include tackling scalability challenges, managing the control plane and developing the new data plane in Rust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about optimizing hardware through software to reduce costs while enhancing user quality, this team offers an exciting opportunity to do that at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering execution within the AV Infrastructure team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition our infrastructure from static scaling to auto-scaling based on demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement the team&#39;s roadmap to enhance reliability and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead the re-architecting of our infrastructure primitives, shifting from bare metal to cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Discord &quot;just works&quot; by building and maintaining reliable, efficient infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience as an Engineering Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked with large-scale distributed systems serving tens or hundreds of millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a hands-on Engineering Manager who embraces technical complexity and understands the entire stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience managing networked video infrastructure or real-time packet-based applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked with cloud environments (e.g., GCP, AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can effectively balance cost considerations against product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working with WebRTC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve explored io_uring based approaches for problems before with your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with Rust or C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve used Discord personally. If you&#39;ve played games and used Go Live with friends, you understand the product&#39;s capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re familiar with DevOps tools such as Salt or Terraform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
